anon <anon@anonn.com> wrote:
>A master lich can cast finger of death,

*Some* master liches (those whose level has been increased due to being
found on a particularly deep dungeon level, or the effects of monster
experience) can cast *touch* of death (a melee attack spell which may,
but is not guaranteed to, kill you if you are neither hallucinating nor
magic-resistant).  Some can't.

*No* monster can cast *finger* of death (a ranged attack spell which
duplicates the effect of zapping a wand of death); that's a player spell.

(Not that the distinction matters *much* where master liches are
concerned, since they are covetous and therefore are usually not in
sight of the player unless they are in melee range.)
